The first adversarial probe exposed an important distinction: a full-graph sequential BFS finds valid packings on every tested instance, so this family cannot masquerade as structurally hard. I’m retaining it only as Track B and moving that successful polynomial routine into the required `reference_algorithm`; the failing panel will now contain only attacks executable from the prompt without enumerating the 625-vertex graph. The hard preset’s planted witness is about 800–1,000 characters and 142–171 local operations.
