+    "difference/suffix-swap edge rule.  Theorem 2.1 fixes k<=l and guarantees "
+    "c=l-ceil(k/2) internally disjoint U-Steiner trees; Algorithm 1 explicitly "
+    "produces them by expanding K_l atoms, so Track A is unavailable.  The easy "
+    "facts to avoid are the paper's polynomial-time result for fixed k and c in "
+    "general graphs (Introduction) and its complete constructive solution on "
+    "Sierpinski graphs (Section 2).  This generator samples terminals uniformly "
