README.md:116:This family is easy with ordinary tools: Algorithm 1 and sequential BFS both solve every audited hard instance. The G4 prior is uniform over bounded, nonempty, globally edge-disjoint sets of genuine graph edges; it does **not** condition each set to be a connected terminal-spanning tree, so 0/200,000 substantially understates the success probability of an informed graph sampler. No ILP, SAT, multicommodity-flow relaxation, or dedicated Steiner-packing package was tried. The canonical key exactly handles terminal reordering and coordinatewise alphabet permutations, the natural automorphisms used here, but does not attempt arbitrary graph-isomorphism canonicalization. Finally, the only tested route to more difficulty was recursive depth; an accepted compact symbolic encoding of long Sierpiński paths could remove the current answer cap and merits a future run.
