441:\section{Proof of Theorem \ref{main}}\label{section-main}
444:We first introduce some notations, operations and auxiliary graphs that are used in the proof. Then we give a transitional theorem (Theorem \ref{Theorem_lower_bond}), which is the main tool for the proof of Theorem \ref{main}.  Theorem \ref{Theorem_lower_bond} will be proved by constructing an algorithm, and the proof takes up almost entire Section \ref{section-main} (the proof is divided into two parts:  the construction of algorithm and the proof of its correctness). 
445:Finally, we complete the proof of  Theorem \ref{main} by using Theorem \ref{Theorem_lower_bond}.
