   470	 \hline
   471	 $u^e,v^e$ & If $e=uv$ is an edge of $G_s$, then $e$ is also an edge of $G_{s-1}$. let $u_e,v_e$ denote endpoints of $e$ in $G_{s-1}$ such that $u_e\in H^u$ and $v_e\in H^v$. \\
   472	 \hline
