   935	
   936	If $s=n$, then each $T_i$ in $G_n$ is the empty graph and the result holds.
   937	Thus, suppose $s\leq n-1$.
   938	Hence, the labelled vertex $v$ of $G_{s+1}$ always exists.
   939	The following implies that the result holds for $s=n-1$. Note that $U^{n-1}=W^{v_{root}}$.
